From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 05:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DRMBackend: pre-rotate layers the plane can't rotate

Where the panel is rotated, gamescope asks the plane to rotate every
layer. A plane that rotates on only a few pipes (one on SM4450), or not
past a line limit, then refuses the frame and all of it is composited on
the GPU. A plane that can't rotate at all composites every frame.

With --composite-blit, copy the layers the plane can't rotate into
panel-oriented buffers with a VK_QCOM_rotated_copy_commands blit and
scan the copies out unrotated, placed as before so the plane still
scales them: the overlays first, so the base keeps a plane that rotates,
then every layer, and every layer when the plane can't rotate at all.
The blits run only once the display takes the layout.

Only when the layers don't fit the planes even then, composite the
overlays into one, drawn in panel orientation, and scan that out beside
the base. A frame that doesn't fit that way either is composited whole.

The blank Steam overlay layer that keeps an overlay plane on is only
painted where turning a plane on is slow, with AMD color management.
Elsewhere it takes a plane the game could use.
---
